> What exactly would you be asserting in `@BeforeEach` or `@AfterEach`?
> Asking because I want to understand the use case.
> We can likely add support for this, but I want to figure out if it's worth it

This is a dumbed down example, but if I have something like this:
```java
@QuarkusTest
class FruitRepositoryTests {
	@Inject
	FruitRepository fruitRepository;

	@BeforeEach
	public void beforeEach() {
				this.fruitRepository.count()
					.subscribe().withSubscriber(UniAssertSubscriber.create())
					.awaitSubscription(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertSubscribed()
					.awaitItem(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertItem(2L)
					.assertCompleted();
	}

	@Test
	public void doTest() {
		assertThat(true).isTrue();
	}
}
```

This works fine, as well as if I have a test which uses `@TestReactiveTransaction` in the mix of tests:
```java
@QuarkusTest
class FruitRepositoryTests {
	@Inject
	FruitRepository fruitRepository;

	@BeforeEach
	public void beforeEach() {
				this.fruitRepository.count()
					.subscribe().withSubscriber(UniAssertSubscriber.create())
					.awaitSubscription(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertSubscribed()
					.awaitItem(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertItem(2L)
					.assertCompleted();
	}

	@Test
	@TestReactiveTransaction
	public void findByName(UniAsserter asserter) {
		asserter.assertThat(() -> this.fruitRepository
			.persist(new Fruit(null, "Grapefruit", "Summer fruit"))
			.replaceWith(this.fruitRepository.findByName("Grapefruit")),
			fruit -> {
				assertThat(fruit)
					.isNotNull()
					.extracting(Fruit::getName, Fruit::getDescription)
					.containsExactly("Grapefruit", "Summer fruit");

				assertThat(fruit.getId())
					.isNotNull()
					.isGreaterThan(2L);
			}
		);
	}
}
```

The `beforeEach` does work. If I move the `@TestReactiveTransaction` to the class instead of on the individual method though, then it doesn't work, and I'm also not able to inject the `UniAsserter` into the `beforeEach` method.
```java
@QuarkusTest
@TestReactiveTransaction
class FruitRepositoryTests {
	@Inject
	FruitRepository fruitRepository;

        @BeforeEach
	public void beforeEachFails(UniAsserter asserter) {
		asserter.assertEquals(this.fruitRepository::count, 2L);
	}

        @BeforeEach
	public void beforeEach2AlsoFails() {
				this.fruitRepository.count()
					.subscribe().withSubscriber(UniAssertSubscriber.create())
					.awaitSubscription(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertSubscribed()
					.awaitItem(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
					.assertItem(2L)
					.assertCompleted();
	}

        @BeforeEach
        public void beforeEach3AlsoFails() {
                var count = this.fruitRepository.count()
			.await().atMost(Duration.ofSeconds(5));
		
		assertThat(count)
			.isEqualTo(2L);
        }

	@Test
	public void findByName(UniAsserter asserter) {
		asserter.assertThat(() -> this.fruitRepository
			.persist(new Fruit(null, "Grapefruit", "Summer fruit"))
			.replaceWith(this.fruitRepository.findByName("Grapefruit")),
			fruit -> {
				assertThat(fruit)
					.isNotNull()
					.extracting(Fruit::getName, Fruit::getDescription)
					.containsExactly("Grapefruit", "Summer fruit");

				assertThat(fruit.getId())
					.isNotNull()
					.isGreaterThan(2L);
			}
		);
	}
}
```

